{{/*
  Ticket template. Go text/template over pkg/ticket.TemplateData.

  The FIRST line must be "Summary: ..."; then a blank line; then the description
  body. Keeping both in one file means the whole wording of a ticket lives in one
  place, editable by whoever owns the process rather than in Go.

  Available:
    .ServiceName .Images .ImageCount .GroupNoun .Refs .Priority
    .Source .SourcePath - the shared change target, present on grouped tickets too
    .Accounts .Namespaces .Teams .WorkloadCount
    .CriticalCount .HighCount .ProviderAssessed
    .FixableCriticals (.ID .CVSS .EPSS .FixedVersion .KEV) .MaxEPSS .KnownExploited
    .Upgrade  - the single version move, or NIL when the grouped images do not
                share one target version (.Kind .Name .Current .Latest .Managed
                .Source .SourcePath .Direct)
    .Upgrades - always populated, one entry per image
                (.Ref .Repo .Current .Latest .Source .SourcePath .Managed .Direct)

  This is an EXAMPLE. Edit it to match how your teams actually work.
*/ -}}
{{- if .Upgrade -}}
Summary: Upgrade {{ .ServiceName }} to {{ .Upgrade.Latest }}
{{- else -}}
Summary: Upgrade {{ .ServiceName }} {{ .GroupNoun }} ({{ .ImageCount }}) to their latest versions
{{- end }}

**Business objective/requirements**

{{ if .Upgrade -}}
Upgrade {{ .ServiceName }} from {{ .Upgrade.Current }} to {{ .Upgrade.Latest }} to clear known container vulnerabilities.
{{- else -}}
Upgrade the {{ .ImageCount }} images below to clear known container vulnerabilities. {{ if .Source }}They are grouped because one change covers them all.{{ else }}They are grouped because they are managed together; each is bumped in its own place, listed below.{{ end }}
{{- end }}

**Technical Requirements & Actions**

{{ range .Upgrades }}* {{ .Repo }}: {{ .Current }} -> {{ .Latest }}{{ if not .Direct }} (version owned by the {{ .Managed }}){{ end }}{{ if and (not $.Source) .Source }}, change in {{ .Source }}{{ if .SourcePath }} path {{ .SourcePath }}{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{ end -}}
{{- if .Source }}* Change target: {{ .Source }}{{ if .SourcePath }} (path: {{ .SourcePath }}){{ end }}
{{ end -}}
* Workloads affected: {{ .WorkloadCount }}{{ if .Namespaces }} in namespace(s) {{ range $i, $n := .Namespaces }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}{{ $n }}{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{ if .Accounts }}* Environments: {{ range $i, $a := .Accounts }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}{{ $a }}{{ end }}
{{ end }}
**Why this is prioritised**

{{ if .ProviderAssessed -}}
Scanner counts: {{ .CriticalCount }} critical, {{ .HighCount }} high. Assessment priority: {{ .Priority }}.
{{- else -}}
NOTE: the scan provider has not assessed these images, so severity counts are unavailable rather than zero. Assessment priority: {{ .Priority }}.
{{- end }}
{{- if .KnownExploited }}

This image carries a CVE in CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalogue (confirmed exploitation in the wild).
{{- else if gt .MaxEPSS 0.5 }}

Highest EPSS across its CVEs is {{ printf "%.2f" .MaxEPSS }}: a high predicted probability of exploitation in the next 30 days.
{{- end }}
{{- with .FixableCriticals }}

Fixable critical CVEs, most exploitable first:

{{ range . }}* {{ .ID }} (CVSS {{ printf "%.1f" .CVSS }}, EPSS {{ printf "%.3f" .EPSS }}){{ if .FixedVersion }} fixed in {{ .FixedVersion }}{{ end }}{{ if .KEV }} - KNOWN EXPLOITED{{ end }}
{{ end -}}
{{- end }}

**Test Strategies**

* Confirm functionality is unchanged after the upgrade.
* Roll to lower environments before production where applicable.

**Acceptance Criteria**

{{ if .Upgrade -}}
{{ .ServiceName }} is running {{ .Upgrade.Latest }} in all environments listed above.
{{- else -}}
Every image listed above is running its latest version in all environments listed above.
{{- end }}
